{
  "pedal": "Boss BF-3 Flanger — focused reamp, both outputs recorded (Output A: the pedal as the model has it; Output B: never measured)",
  "comment": "Guitar excerpts (captures/di/) over a steady 8 kHz sine 30 dB under the guitar's peak (the probe: on the output it is the dry plus the flanged copy, so its level and phase trace the delay at every moment, guitar or not). Most guitar takes at -12 dB: the pedal's output clips a little over a guitar's peak and a flanger's peaks add 7 dB, so full level is kept for the takes that are about the clip (funk). Depth 7:00 first (the delay stands still: tone, level and timing of the flanged copy against the waveform, Res's loop, three Manual positions — which of NAM-X's two Standard models is closer in the bass), then the sweep: each setting's probe alone and guitar over it, one take twice (the pedal against itself), the lead held out of any fit; Res under a moving delay; the fast rates; then ULTRA. A plug in Output B doesn't change Output A (the October study). Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. Takes ordered so each step turns one or two knobs.",
  "quiet_dbfs": -60,
  "both_outputs": true,
  "knobs": [
    "Mode",
    "Manual",
    "Res",
    "Depth",
    "Rate"
  ],
